step 1:

Ingestion Layer (Raw / Bronze)
Source: Data is loaded from Azure Data Lake Storage (ADLS Gen2 / Blob) or Unity Catalog Volumes:
Iot telemetry.csv: Contains high-frequency operational measurements (timestamp, site_id, building_id, asset_id, sensor_id, temperature, humidity, pressure, vibration, power_consumption, operating_mode).
Event.csv: Contains discrete alert logs (event_id, timestamp, asset_id, event_type, severity, message).

functions used: PySpark reads the CSV files using .option("header", "true") and .option("inferSchema", "true") into distributed Spark DataFrames.

step 2:

Validation & Quality Control Layer (Silver Cleaning)
Before processing calculations, the data is sanitized against four core criteria:
Duplicate Handling: Drops duplicate sensor records based on [timestamp, asset_id, sensor_id] and duplicate event records based on event_id.
Data Type Normalization: Formats timestamp strings into structured Spark SQL TIMESTAMP objects using F.to_timestamp().
Null & Blank Value Removal: Filters out records with missing IDs (asset_id, site_id, building_id), invalid timestamp entries, or critical missing telemetry metrics (e.g., null power consumption).
Referential Integrity: Ensures asset IDs in both datasets are non-empty and logically sound.

step 3:

Transforms the granular data into standardized business metrics.
Hourly Energy Consumption & Environmental Conditions:
Groups telemetry data into 1-hour time windows using F.date_trunc("hour", "timestamp").
Computes total hourly energy consumed (hourly_energy_consumption_kWh = SUM(power_consumption)).
Computes environmental averages (avg_temperature_C, avg_humidity_pct, avg_pressure_hPa, avg_vibration).
Daily Asset Utilization:
Groups data by calendar day (F.to_date()).
Calculates the percentage of time an asset was operational (RUNNING / ACTIVE) versus total reporting intervals.

step 4:

Data Aggregation Layer (Gold Business Metrics)
Summarizes the transformed data into a 3-level operational hierarchy:
Asset-Level Metrics (asset_metrics):
Summarizes lifetime/period energy consumption, overall average temperatures, and humidity per asset.
Joins with fault_statistics so asset health and reliability can be monitored in one place.
Building-Level Metrics (building_metrics):
Aggregates energy usage and environment conditions at the building level.
Calculates total active assets per building (COUNT(DISTINCT asset_id)).\
Site-Level Metrics (site_metrics):
High-level rollup representing facility-wide power demand, environmental conditions, total buildings, and total assets.

step 5:

Storage, Serving & Orchestration
Delta / Parquet Persistence: Results are written in overwrite mode to Delta tables in Unity Catalog (dataworkspace.default.*) and Azure Blob Storage (curated/).
Automation (Workflows): The pipeline is packaged inside a Databricks Job task that runs on a schedule (e.g., hourly/daily) using Serverless compute, ensuring the data model refreshes automatically without manual intervention.
